{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136066-converting-and-expanding-npcs-from-danse-de-la-mort-chronicle-2nd-ed","id":1136066,"title":"Converting and expanding NPCs from Danse de la Mort Chronicle (2nd Ed.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-31T19:58:49-07:00","id":1136066,"title":"Converting and expanding NPCs from Danse de la Mort Chronicle (2nd Ed.)","content":"Hoi,<br /> <br /> I am running the free <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?term=danse+de+&amp;test_epoch=0&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Danse de la Mort Chronicle</a> using the 2nd Edition rules and I want to share the stats I use for some of the NPCs. Please let me know what you think! Not sure how well I updated/expanded the characters. I will start with one NPC and then add others as I finish assigning the stats to them.<br /> <br /> Contains spoilers for Danse de la Mort. <hr /><b>Alexander</b><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Lancea et Sanctum<br /> <b>Mask</b>: Rebel<br /> <b>Dirge</b>: Conformist<br /> <b>Humanity</b>: 4<br /> <b>Touchstones</b>: 1978 Dodge Aspen coupe (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dodge_Aspen\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dodge_Aspen</a>)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills</b>: Academics 1, Investigation 2 (Vampires), Occult 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills</b>: Brawl 3 (Breaking Bones), Drive 1, Firearms 3, Larceny 2 (Picking Locks), Stealth 3, Survival 3, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills</b>: Intimidation 3, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Status (NOLA) 1; Status (Lancea et Sanctum) 1; Riding the Wave 3; Resources 1; Cacophony Savvy 1; Safe Place 2; Herd 1<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 14<br /> <b>Blood Potency</b>: 4<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Celerity 2, Protean 3, Resilience 3, Vigor 2<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative Modifier</b>: 6<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 5<br /> <br /> There is little information about Alexander. I didn't find him in the 1st edition chapter on NOLA. The City of the Damned, New Orleans didn't help either. Looks like he is just a character created for Danse de la Mort.<br /> <br /> I wanted the stats to show an unassuming bone-breaker for Vidal. The chronicle suggests using his stats for Vidal's guards at one point, so that seems fitting.<br /> <br /> Not sure why the chronicle gives him BP 4... Vidal authorizes the protagonists to Diablerise some characters at two points in the story, so that seems like one justification. Would love to hear your ideas.<br /> <br /> He is a bald guy in leather pants, so I kinda felt that he is trying to project that Rebel aura when it comes to mortals. However, he is clearly just a guy working for Vidal, who doesn't want trouble, so Conformist seems fitting. There are few details about him in the chronicle, so I decided to use what little the chronicle mentions (albeit in passing) as his touchstone. I chose a specific car to augment the Rebel thing a bit.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the Merits, but he is supposed to be a somewhat well-adjusted Kindred with some good leg-breaking skills.<br /> <hr /> <b>Andrea Ouellette</b><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Nosferatu<br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Ordo Dracul<br /> <b>Mask</b>: Martyr (&quot;I might be a monster, but I have no loyalty to monstrosity&quot; is her mantra)<br /> <b>Dirge</b>: Visionary (Andrea works and experiments on controlling her monstrous urges. She wants to share that with Edward and wanted to participate in Sarah's experiment)<br /> <b>Humanity</b>: 5<br /> <b>Touchstones</b>: The Orphan (the base Touchstone, Spouse, is lost)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills</b>: Academics 1, Computer 1, Occult 3 (Research), Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills</b>: Athletics 2, Brawl 2 (Sucker Punch), Drive 2, Firearms 1, Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills</b>: Empathy 3, Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Streetwise 3 (Avoiding Trouble)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Status (NOLA) 1, Status (Ordo Dracul) 1, Language (French) 1, Language (Spanish) 1, Safe Place 2, Haven 1, Riding the Wave 2, Touchstone 1<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 12<br /> <b>Blood Potency</b>: 4<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Auspex 1, Nightmare 3, Resilience 1, Vigor 1, Mystery of the Wyrm 3<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative Modifier</b>: 5 <b>Defense</b>: 5 (Reinforced clothing 1/0)<br /> <br /> I have added Mystery of the Wyrm to Andrea as in the original chronicle her Coils are not mentioned. The chronicle mentions that she strives to control her Beast, so Wyrm seems like a good fit.<br /> <br /> For the Touchstones I decided to avoid coming up with details and instead just referred to the ones in the book. This way there is something to work off if the players come digging, but I don't have to put too much work into it. <hr /><br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","user":"Chubby Russian","date":".  Added Andrea Ouellette 09-11-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:18:46-07:00","id":1138688,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Power Level as found in the New Orleans Book. I find his Blood Potency to high also his physical attributes. I rather make him an expendable Hound of BP 2(Maybe he\u00b4s also Daeva and Father Marrows Childe), thus an experienced Neonate. <br /> I used the Campaign but set it in Chicago and used &quot;Loki&quot; as the Alexander replacement.<br /> I\u00b4d make more of a charming leg breaker. Big rough older brother type. <br /> Riding the Wave 3 makes him very dangerous. And i don\u00b4t think he need so much of Protean 1 or even none would be enough, instead give him one level of Dominate so he can defuse things without breaking bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:16:29-07:00","id":1139465,"title":"","content":"maekkel,<br /> <br /> Thank you for your input. I am trying to run the game as close to the written source as possible, so I am a bit hesitant to make extensive changes... <br /> <br /> My thought is that his BP is so high to wake up PCs from torpor if something happens, especially during Fury. Also the adventure mentions him waking up Father Marrow with his blood, so his BP needs to be at least high enough to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> His attributes are only that high due to his Disciplines: the base ones are only 4/3/3, which is not too high for an experienced Neonate. What do you think his Attributes should be?<br /> <br /> I gave him Riding the Wave 3 as a substitute for not being able to deal Agg with claws. The Agg from claws is an important point in the fight during Fury - he should be able to beat Andrea (or ruin the PCs' day if he succumbs to the Blood Rage). Better than giving him Claws of the Unholy I think.<br /> <br /> Why do you think he shouldn't have Protean? I think more than enough NPCs in that chronicle have Dominate, giving it to a Hound would be a bit of an overkill. Majesty maybe?<br /> <br /> Regarding you personal game, how did using Loki work for you? I though Loki was with the Circle. Or did you change the whole city to the canon Chicago court?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}